        ":question/id": "2ed50138-474a-54c5-b601-b5f1bfa8af7f",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(-165^\\circ\\right)$ without using a calculator?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $-165^\\circ=60^\\circ-225^\\circ$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(-165^\\circ\\right) &=\\sin\\left(60^\\circ-225^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(225^\\circ\\right)-\\cos\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
